```python
def batch_stream(iterable, batch_size: int):
    batch = []
    for item in iterable:
        batch.append(item)
        if len(batch) == batch_size:
            yield batch
            batch = []
    if batch:
        yield batch
```
This lazily consumes the input iterable and produces discrete batches in O(batch_size) memory.
